 "notes": "U(1)_{B-L} gauge boson dark matter search with KAGRA O3GK auxiliary length channels (MICH blue, PRCL orange). Headline 95% upper limit on epsilon_{B-L} = gauge coupling normalized by e, from Fig.5 (raster upperlimits_final.png; no ancillary data). Reported epsilon_{B-L} directly as g_BL per compilation convention for B-L vector-DM papers (Michimura/Miller/LIGO-O3 family; no *e factor). x-axis converted from frequency via m_A=h*f (m_A[eV]=4.1357e-15*f[Hz]); calibrated x-ticks px156/504/853=10/100/1000 Hz, y-ticks py105..468=1e-15..1e-19. Data span 15-1015 Hz => 6.2e-14..4.2e-12 eV. Curve = lower envelope (10th-pct floor per log-f bin) of combined MICH+PRCL best constraint, rejecting upward line-artifact spikes; deepest ~2.5e-20 near 100-150 Hz (m_A~4e-13 eV), rising to ~3e-19 at high mass. Paper notes these limits are weaker than Eot-Wash/MICROSCOPE by orders of magnitude but are its own measured bound. rho_DM~0.4 GeV/cm^3, v_vir~220 km/s SHM.",
